Harsh Kausalyā words recall past misdeed --- Burning with double grief Daśaratha begs favor --- Daśaratha calls husband visible god to wives --- Daśaratha bids grieved Kausalyā speak no harshness --- Weeping Kausalyā begs pardon at his feet --- Kausalyā says grief destroys all worse than foes --- Rāma fifth night seems five years to her --- Kausalyā says grief swells like river-fed sea --- Night falls as Kausalyā speaks --- Soothed king sinks into sleep grief-seized